            <ArticleTitle>Off-pump coronary artery bypass combined with abdominal aortic aneurysm repair in an 88-year-old male.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of an 88-year-old patient who underwent off-pump coronary artery bypass using an aortic connector followed by repair of an abdominal aortic aneurysm to reduce surgical invasiveness. This approach merits consideration for high-risk patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
